// Bosses that are creatures in their own right.
//
// A spawn group can name a boss inline - boss_type names a species and
// boss_health multiplies its numbers - and most of them do. That kind of boss
// is a bigger, tougher one of something already in the group.
//
// A block here is the other kind: a boss with its own creature definition in
// creatures.txt, marked `boss: 1` there so nothing else can spawn it. A group
// reaches it by naming the block rather than a species.
//
//   type:          the creature in creatures.txt
//   health:        multiplies that creature's own health
//   strength_min,
//   strength_max:  register 023. How powerful a version of itself this one
//                  turns out to be, rolled once per spawn and applied to its
//                  health, both combat levels, its damage and its drawn size.
//                  Equal values are a fixed statblock.
//
// The rest of a block is the fight - what the boss does about losing it. A
// boss with none of it is a statblock with a large health bar, which is a
// long fight rather than a hard one. These are what make it answer back, and
// both of them run out, because a boss that could heal or summon forever is
// a wall rather than a fight:
//
//   weapon:        one line per piece of gear, worn in the order written
//                  instead of the random loadout every other creature rolls.
//                  More weapons than there are hands is allowed and is the
//                  reason this is a list: the first takes the slot its kind
//                  wears and the rest go into slots that name nothing on the
//                  body, so they still count for damage and still fire their
//                  on-hit effects. Ordinary equipment validation is on the
//                  path where a *player* equips something and never sees
//                  these, so nothing has to be relaxed to allow it.
//   heal:          health restored each time a blow lands on it, and
//   heal_charges:  how many times it can do that. The amount moves with the
//                  strength roll like everything else; the charges do not,
//                  so a bigger Warden is not a longer stalemate.
//   summon:        the creature it calls, and
//   summon_at:     `<share of its health> | <how many>`, one line per stage
//                  of the fight. Shares of the bar rather than amounts of
//                  it, because the bar is not known until the boss rolls -
//                  an amount would name a different moment every spawn.
//                  Each stage fires once, highest share first.
//   summon_budget: the pool every stage draws from. Defaults to exactly
//                  enough for all of them, so it is worth writing only to
//                  make the last stage a real one that can come up short.
//
// A second boss is a second block. Nothing here is reached by name in the
// server: a group that wants this behaviour names a block instead of a
// species, and a block that wants it writes these lines.


// --- Gauntlet bosses ---
// The eight gauntlet courts. Each heals on the blow and calls its region
// up out of the ground in three stages, the biggest kept for the end.

[boss]
name: Boar King of the Resin Road
type: boar_king
health: 1.0
strength_min: 0.9
strength_max: 1.6
difficulty: 44

heal: 18
heal_charges: 30

summon: brambleback_boar
summon_at: 0.75 | 3
summon_at: 0.45 | 3
summon_at: 0.2 | 4
summon_budget: 10
[/boss]

